# 03 · Performance

## Performance Approach
- Measure before optimizing.
- Define and track meaningful performance budgets (latency, startup, memory, CPU, frame time, throughput).
- Prioritize end-user impact and system reliability.

## Common Rules
- Avoid expensive work on critical user/request paths.
- Cache intentionally with explicit invalidation rules.
- Batch/chunk large operations where possible.
- Prefer async/non-blocking execution for I/O-bound work.

## UI-Facing Systems
- Keep rendering/update paths lightweight.
- Limit unnecessary rerenders/recompositions/layout passes.
- Use lazy loading and virtualization for large lists or datasets.
- Profile jank, startup, and memory with platform tooling.

## API/Service Systems
- Set clear timeouts and retry policies.
- Use pagination/streaming for large payloads.
- Control fan-out and concurrency to avoid cascading failures.
- Track p50/p95/p99 latency and error rates by endpoint.

## Validation
- Benchmark/profiling evidence is required for performance-sensitive changes.
- Regressions should block release until accepted or mitigated.
